#: ../contents/ui/AirAndSolarItem.qml
msgid ""
"The AQI is a measure of air quality that takes into account the levels of various pollutants in the air. It ranges from 0 to 500, with higher values indicating worse air quality. An AQI of 0-50 is "
"considered good, 51-100 is moderate, 101-150 is unhealthy for sensitive groups, 151-200 is unhealthy, 201-300 is very unhealthy, and 301-500 is hazardous."
msgstr ""

#: ../contents/ui/AirAndSolarItem.qml
msgid ""
"The AQHI is a measure of how the air quality may affect human health. It ranges from 1 to 10+, with higher values indicating more unfavorable conditions for health. An AQHI of 1-3 is considered low "
"risk, 4-6 is moderate risk, 7-10 is high risk, and 10+ is very high risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../contents/ui/AirAndSolarItem.qml
msgctxt "Particulate Matter"
msgid "PM2.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../contents/ui/AirAndSolarItem.qml
msgid ""
"Particulate matter (PM2.5) is a measure of the amount of solid particles and liquid droplets suspended in the air. It can have serious health effects, especially on the respiratory and "
"cardiovascular systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../contents/ui/AirAndSolarItem.qml
msgid "Solar info"
msgstr ""

#: ../contents/ui/AirAndSolarItem.qml
